---
description: Core data-flow architecture for the elixir project — enforced on every file in lib/data/ and lib/src/.
alwaysApply: true
---

## Canonical data flow

```
UI  (lib/src/<feature>/)
 └─> Provider  (lib/data/providers/<domain>_provider.dart)
      ├─> [default]  Client  (lib/data/services/clients/<domain>_client.dart)
      ├─> [when repo exists]  Repository  (lib/data/repositories/<domain>_repository.dart)  ->  Client
      └─> [when needed]  DataSources  (lib/data/db/, lib/data/shared_preference/, lib/data/hubs/)
```

**Providers call Retrofit clients directly by default.** A repository is added only when the domain already has one, or when introducing one is justified (non-trivial mapping, multi-client orchestration, or a local cache layer).

Current domains that have a repository (providers for these must go through the repository):
- `posts` — `lib/data/repositories/posts_repository.dart`
- `user` — `lib/data/repositories/user_repoistory.dart` (typo in filename is intentional — matches disk)
- `attachment` — `lib/data/repositories/attachment_repository.dart`
- `notifications` — `lib/data/repositories/notifications_repository.dart`

All other domains: provider -> client is the expected, correct path.

## Swagger controller → file naming

For each Swagger controller use one matching `snake_case` base name (e.g. `Auth` → `auth`):

| Layer | Path | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Retrofit client | `lib/data/services/clients/<name>_client.dart` | `auth_client.dart` |
| Riverpod provider | `lib/data/providers/<name>_provider.dart` | `auth_provider.dart` |
| Repository | `lib/data/repositories/<name>_repository.dart` *(only when justified)* | `posts_repository.dart` |

Do not add a separate provider file per UI page or UI step. Put related notifiers in the same domain `*_provider.dart` file — multiple `@riverpod` classes in one file is fine.

## Layer rules

### Provider (`lib/data/providers/`)
- Use `@riverpod` codegen + `part '*.g.dart'` — do not hand-write providers.
- Call repository if one exists for the domain; otherwise call the Retrofit client directly.
- Never call datasources directly from a provider.
- Never import from `lib/src/` (no UI types, no `BuildContext`, no `ThemeData`).
- Expose immutable state only; all mutations happen inside notifier methods.

### Retrofit client (`lib/data/services/clients/`)
- Stateless: typed HTTP endpoints only, no business logic.
- All Retrofit clients live under `lib/data/services/clients/`. Do not create a parallel `lib/data/clients/` folder.
- Shared Retrofit helpers (Dio module, interceptors, converters) stay in `lib/data/services/http/` and `lib/data/services/interceptors/`.

### Repository (`lib/data/repositories/`) — optional
- Exists only for domains listed above, or when added for a justified reason.
- Owns: calling clients, mapping API models → feature models, normalising errors.
- Must not import from `lib/src/`.

### Datasources (`lib/data/db/`, `lib/data/shared_preference/`, `lib/data/hubs/`)
- Low-level persistence/transport only.
- No transformations, no UI awareness.

## Mapping rule
- UI must never consume raw API models from `lib/data/models/`.
- Map in the provider (default) or in the repository (when one exists).
- Feature-facing types may live in `lib/src/<feature>/models/` only when a dedicated UI shape is needed and it does not duplicate `lib/data/models/`.

## Forbidden patterns
- UI calling a Retrofit client or datasource directly.
- A provider calling a datasource directly (bypass provider -> repository path when repo exists).
- API models imported in `lib/src/` widget files.
- Repository importing from `lib/src/`.
- New abstraction layers: no `usecases/`, `controllers/`, `managers/`, or `viewmodels/` folders anywhere.
- Placing providers under `lib/src/<feature>/` — providers belong in `lib/data/providers/` only.
